  "rgb-to-hex-converter": {
    whatItIs: `RGB to HEX Converter translates RGB (Red, Green, Blue) decimal channel values into standard 6-character hexadecimal color codes (#RRGGBB). For example, inputting the channel values 59, 130, 246 converts directly into #3B82F6.

Web designers, front-end developers, and digital artists constantly convert color specifications between RGB notation (commonly produced by browser dev tools, Canvas 2D image analysis, and photo editing software) and hexadecimal format. Hex color codes are the universal standard for CSS stylesheets, Tailwind configuration files, SVG definitions, and design tokens in Figma and Sketch.

## How Decimal Channels Map to Hex Bytes

Each RGB channel is an 8-bit integer with an intensity ranging from 0 (minimum intensity) to 255 (maximum intensity):
- Red channel: decimal 0–255 becomes a 2-digit hex byte (00 to FF).
- Green channel: decimal 0–255 becomes a 2-digit hex byte (00 to FF).
- Blue channel: decimal 0–255 becomes a 2-digit hex byte (00 to FF).

For example, pure white (255, 255, 255) maps to FF, FF, FF (#FFFFFF), and black (0, 0, 0) maps to 00, 00, 00 (#000000). This converter processes your comma-separated channel inputs in real time, validating ranges and rendering an interactive preview swatch instantly.`,
    features: [
      `Converts decimal Red, Green, and Blue channel values (0–255) into clean uppercase 6-digit hex color strings (#RRGGBB)`,
      `Real-time interactive color swatch displaying the rendered color preview instantly`,
      `Flexible comma-separated input format accepting variable spacing (e.g. 255, 100, 50)`,
      `One-click clipboard copy for pasting into CSS stylesheets, Tailwind configs, and HTML attributes`,
      `Immediate input validation preventing invalid channel values outside the 0–255 range`,
      `100% client-side computation running entirely in your browser with zero remote transmission`,
    ],
    howToUse: {
      name: `How to convert RGB channel values to a hexadecimal color code`,
      steps: [
        { name: `Enter RGB Channel Values`, text: `Type three comma-separated numbers between 0 and 255 into the input box (for example, 59, 130, 246).` },
        { name: `Check Live Color Swatch`, text: `Verify the rendered color preview box and the calculated uppercase #RRGGBB string.` },
        { name: `Copy Hex Code`, text: `Click Copy to copy the hex color string to your clipboard for your stylesheet or design system.` },
      ],
    },
    faqs: [
      { question: `How are RGB decimal numbers converted to a hexadecimal color code?`, answer: `Each color channel (0 to 255) is converted to a base-16 number using toString(16), padded with a leading zero if needed to ensure two digits. Combining the red, green, and blue pairs yields the 6-character hex code.` },
      { question: `What happens if a channel value exceeds 255 or is negative?`, answer: `Valid 8-bit color channels must fall between 0 and 255. If a value is negative, exceeds 255, or contains non-numeric characters, the tool displays 'Invalid'.` },
      { question: `Does the output include the hash (#) symbol?`, answer: `Yes. The converter outputs the standard CSS format including the leading hash, such as #FF6432.` },
      { question: `Can I convert HEX color codes back into RGB?`, answer: `Yes. Use the companion HEX to RGB Converter to translate hexadecimal strings back into functional rgb(r, g, b) notation.` },
      { question: `Does this tool track or send color queries to an external server?`, answer: `No. All color math runs entirely inside your browser's local JavaScript runtime.` },
    ],
    seoDescription: `Convert RGB color values (0–255) to 6-digit hexadecimal codes (#RRGGBB) online. Free client-side RGB to hex converter with live color preview and one-click copy.`,
  },
